# Optical insets

- Follow `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` → Optical insets and `packages/styles/src/inset.css`.
- Measure icons by the full square slot/viewBox, never by visible path bounds.
  Use the same placement for horizontal, vertical, round and asymmetric marks.
  Do not change vendored SVG geometry, scale a chevron separately or add per-icon nudges.
- Center text using the font's cap-to-baseline reference, consistently for every label.
  Use the documented text slots; keep symmetric safety space for accents and descenders.
  Never measure a word to change its padding; wording must not alter placement.
- For a fixed-height backplate H and an edge item's reference height B, the outer
  inset is (H − B) / 2. CSS padding subtracts the border width exactly once.
  Calculate start and end independently; an end chevron follows the leading-icon rule.
- Swatches, dots, avatars, shortcuts and nested buttons use their own box dimensions.
  A content-sized or multiline container uses equal padding around the content group;
  intentional full-width layout can add interior space, not move edge slots off-grid.
- Multiline icon/text: keep the icon's top and leading insets equal, align its center
  with the first text line's cap center, and allow more space below. Preserve leading
  between lines and between a title and description; never center on the whole paragraph.
- Use the same tier's icon, text and gap tokens across Button, Input, Select, Chip and
  Segmented. Menu/Nav and Alert/Toast use the medium UI pairing. Keep icons on the
  12/16/24px ramp and weights unmodified; status dots and keyboard glyphs have distinct
  semantic roles. No per-glyph scaling, stroke adjustments or nudges.
- Keep dimensions token-derived, account for nested density and RTL, and preserve
  component outer heights, line wrapping, native editing, focus and hit targets.
- Add slot selectors to the manifest and mirror markup in React and framework-free docs.
- Verify `inset.html` and the gallery at both densities, all tiers, all font presets,
  RTL, strong borders and narrow widths. Check actual geometry and inspect the preview.
